    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "url": "https://xquik.com/api/v1/x/tweets/search",
        "sendQuery": true,
        "queryParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "q",
              "value": "={{ $json.query }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "limit",
              "value": "={{ $json.limit }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "sendHeaders": true,
        "headerParameters": {
          "parameters": [
            {
              "name": "x-api-key",
              "value": "={{ $env.XQUIK_API_KEY }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "be569443-c727-4c9d-9f9e-273198d8ee16",
      "name": "Search Xquik posts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        700,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Set XQUIK_API_KEY in the n8n environment before running. If environment access is disabled, replace the expression with an n8n Header Auth credential."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const candidates = [$json.data, $json.tweets, $json.results, $json.items];\nconst tweets = candidates.find((value) => Array.isArray(value));\n\nif (!tweets) {\n  return [{ json: { rawResponse: $json } }];\n}\n\nreturn tweets.map((tweet) => ({\n  json: {\n    id: tweet.id ?? tweet.tweetId ?? tweet.restId,\n    text: tweet.text ?? tweet.fullText,\n    url: tweet.url,\n    author: tweet.author?.username ?? tweet.username ?? tweet.screenName,\n    likeCount: tweet.likeCount ?? tweet.favoriteCount,\n    retweetCount: tweet.retweetCount,\n    replyCount: tweet.replyCount\n  }\n}));"
      },
      "id": "bc5f5761-72ed-464b-913f-2ad165281832",
      "name": "Normalize tweet rows",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        940,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Emits one n8n item per post for sheets, alerts, or dashboards."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Xquik X search\n\nSet `XQUIK_API_KEY` in your n8n environment. If `$env` access is disabled, replace the header expression with an n8n Header Auth credential. Change `query` and `limit`, then run manually. The last node emits one item per post for downstream steps.\n\n[API documentation](https://docs.xquik.com/api-reference/overview)\n\nXquik is a closed-source hosted service. Xquik is an independent third-party service. Not affiliated with X Corp. \"Twitter\" and \"X\" are trademarks of X Corp.",
